        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പലഹാരം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പലഹാരം — palahāraṁ — \"a snack\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പലഹാരം (palahāraṁ) from Sanskrit phalāhāra, \"eating fruit\", reshaped as a tadbhava, with Malayalam's noun ending -ṁ (CDIAL 9060). Its parts are phala, \"fruit\", and āhāra, \"food\"; Malayalam softened the ph and widened the sense to any light snack."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
