              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പഴംപൊരി (paḻampori) is native Dravidian, \"fried fruit\": paḻam, \"ripe fruit\" (DEDR 4004), and pori, from the verb \"to fry, parch\" (DEDR 4537, with Tamil pori). DEDR 4004 compares Sanskrit phala."
